{"lines": ["Eleven people vanished in the Andes, and their last radio word was STENDEC.", "August nineteen forty-seven. A British airliner called Star Dust flies from Buenos Aires toward Santiago, Chile.", "At five forty-one, its radio operator taps out a routine Morse message: arriving at five forty-five.", "But he adds one more word: S, T, E, N, D, E, C. Santiago asks again, and the plane sends it twice more.", "Nothing else is ever heard. Search planes find no trace, and for over fifty years, Star Dust is simply gone.", "In nineteen ninety-eight, climbers find an engine in a glacier on Mount Tupungato. Investigators think an avalanche buried the wreck within seconds.", "They now believe the crew misjudged their position in cloud. But nobody has ever decoded STENDEC.", "Was it the word descent, scrambled by thin air, or Morse sent too fast above the Andes?"], "words": [["Eleven", 0.0, 0.18], ["people", 0.18, 0.62], ["vanished", 0.62, 0.96], ["in", 0.96, 1.42], ["the", 1.42, 1.54], ["Andes,", 1.54, 1.94], ["and", 2.2, 2.34], ["their", 2.34, 2.46], ["last", 2.46, 2.72], ["radio", 2.72, 3.3], ["word", 3.3, 3.68], ["was", 3.68, 4.04], ["STENDEC.", 4.04, 4.56], ["August", 4.92, 5.098], ["nineteen", 5.098, 5.374], ["forty-seven.", 5.374, 5.718], ["A", 6.078, 6.238], ["British", 6.238, 6.458], ["airliner", 6.458, 6.918], ["called", 6.918, 7.438], ["Star", 7.438, 7.798], ["Dust", 7.798, 8.158], ["flies", 8.438, 8.798], ["from", 8.798, 9.218], ["Buenos", 9.218, 9.458], ["Aires", 9.458, 10.138], ["toward", 10.138, 10.778], ["Santiago,", 10.778, 11.398], ["Chile.", 11.658, 11.818], ["At", 12.178, 12.24], ["five", 12.24, 12.453], ["forty-one,", 12.453, 12.88], ["its", 13.14, 13.36], ["radio", 13.36, 13.68], ["operator", 13.68, 14.16], ["taps", 14.16, 14.6], ["out", 14.6, 14.92], ["a", 14.92, 15.16], ["routine", 15.16, 15.4], ["Morse", 15.4, 15.84], ["message:", 15.84, 16.4], ["arriving", 16.66, 17.02], ["at", 17.02, 17.38], ["five", 17.38, 17.626], ["forty-five.", 17.626, 18.